& [BoundaryFormation] separates policy from observation
  + [inside] exact caller-supplied entry kind, attributes, directory case flags, component, and component bound
  + [inside] pure deterministic validation and exact UTF-8 order-key projection
  + [outside] acquiring, authenticating, timing, correlating, or physically interpreting any input
  + [outside] stream parsing, traversal, Git reconciliation, topology receipt, admission, mutation, seal, and promotion
  + [correction_only] authority lineage changes while profile semantics and production behavior remain unchanged

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-WEP-001] bind strict profile, strict JSON, source snapshot, and governing correction source
  + [M2B-WEP-002] preserve exact Windows attribute constants and closed known-bit classification
  + [M2B-WEP-003] require DIRECTORY and permit only the exact directory mask for directory kind
  + [M2B-WEP-004] admit exactly NORMAL alone or one nonzero benign subset for regular-file kind
  + [M2B-WEP-005] require supplied case flags Some(0) for directory and None for regular file
  + [M2B-WEP-006] measure exact component length in UTF-16 units under a caller bound from 1 through 32767
  + [M2B-WEP-007] reject forbidden scalars, terminal space, and terminal period
  + [M2B-WEP-008] reject empty, dot, dot-dot, and ASCII-case-insensitive .git components
  + [M2B-WEP-009] reject fixed, numbered, superscript, mixed-case, and extension-bearing reserved device stems
  + [M2B-WEP-010] preserve exact Unicode scalar sequence without normalization and derive exact UTF-8 byte order
  + [M2B-WEP-011] preserve zero dependency, zero unsafe, and zero runtime-effect boundaries
  + [M2B-WEP-012] preserve closed faults, exhaustive proof, rollback, and mandatory nonclaims
  + [M2B-WEP-013] supersede the prior non-governing signature without erasing it
  + [M2B-WEP-014] revalidate the unchanged implementation and evidence under the governing replacement signature

& [DataDesignModel] is one closed pure transform
  + [EntryKind] is directory or regular_file
  + [EntryPolicyInput] is profile, kind, exact attributes, optional directory case flags, exact component, and maximum UTF-16 units
  + [EntryPolicyDecision] preserves profile, kind, attributes, case flags, component, and lowercase hexadecimal exact UTF-8 order key
  + [EntryPolicyFault] is one closed code, field, and bounded deterministic reason
  + [lifecycle] is supplied input to validation to one decision or one fault
  + [state] is absent
  + [provenance] is caller-supplied syntax only and does not become physical evidence
  - never: release a partial decision

& [AttributeTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [READONLY] is 0x00000001
  + [HIDDEN] is 0x00000002
  + [SYSTEM] is 0x00000004
  + [DIRECTORY] is 0x00000010
  + [ARCHIVE] is 0x00000020
  + [NORMAL] is 0x00000080
  + [NOT_CONTENT_INDEXED] is 0x00002000
  + [benign_mask] is 0x00002027
  + [directory_allowed_mask] is 0x00002037
  + [directory] requires DIRECTORY and no bit outside directory_allowed_mask
  + [regular_normal] is exactly NORMAL
  + [regular_marked] is a nonzero subset of benign_mask
  + [all_other_values] reject

& [ComponentTruthTable] is exact
  + [forbidden_scalars] are NUL, U+0001 through U+001F, less-than, greater-than, colon, quote, slash, backslash, vertical-bar, question-mark, and asterisk
  + [terminal_rejection] is trailing space or period
  + [navigation_rejection] is dot or dot-dot
  + [Git_control_rejection] is .git by ordinal ASCII case-insensitive equality
  + [fixed_devices] are CON, PRN, AUX, and NUL before the first period
  + [numbered_devices] are COM1 through COM9 and LPT1 through LPT9 before the first period
  + [superscript_devices] are COM or LPT followed by superscript one, two, or three before the first period
  + [Unicode] is exact and unnormalized

& [ConstraintLedger] is fail closed
  + [C-01] original and correction sources remain byte-bound and separate from derived artifacts
  + [C-02] profile remains cantor-windows-entry-policy/0.1
  + [C-03] production code and behavior remain unchanged during authority correction
  + [C-04] attribute admission is an exhaustive truth table, not a permissive unknown-bit filter
  + [C-05] case-field presence follows kind exactly
  + [C-06] component bounds and namespace hazards reject before decision release
  + [C-07] Unicode normalization, locale casing, and lossy conversion are absent
  + [C-08] order-key bytes are exact UTF-8 bytes
  + [C-09] faults release no partial accepted value
  + [C-10] Cargo, lockfile, dependency, unsafe, and effect deltas are zero
  + [C-11] observation and physical-provenance claims are absent
  + [C-12] old authority is preserved as superseded, not rewritten

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] is source grounded
  + [attributes] originate in AttributeIntent and weave to exhaustive unit tests
  + [case_flags] originate in AttributeIntent and weave to entry-kind relation tests
  + [component] originates in NameIntent and weaves to scalar, terminal, navigation, Git, and device tests
  + [ordering] originates in NameIntent and weaves to exact-byte output tests
  + [faults] originate in fail-closed intent and weave to strict JSON plus no-partial-result behavior
  + [authority] originates in ObservedFault and weaves to the canonical supersession and binding table

& [CrossWeaveTrace] joins existing fabric
  + [topology_forms] supplies kind vocabulary but receives no new physical claim
  + [topology_scanner_formation] requires later policy use but receives no scanner authority
  + [stream_parser] is a sibling pure prerequisite and not an input to this transform
  + [supplied_observation_assembly] may consume the decision only after corrected authority revalidation
  + [evidence_manifest] binds source, canonical, module, tests, solution, proof, and narrative without becoming authority

& [FailureModeSet] is explicit
  + [F-01] source or correction bytes drift
  + [F-02] prior signature is silently relabeled valid
  + [F-03] replacement signature omits stage evidence
  + [F-04] profile or behavior changes during governance repair
  + [F-05] unknown attribute bit admits
  + [F-06] NORMAL combines with another regular-file bit
  + [F-07] kind and case-field relation diverge
  + [F-08] reserved or navigation component admits
  + [F-09] Unicode normalizes or order bytes change
  + [F-10] partial decision escapes
  + [F-11] dependency, unsafe, or runtime effect appears
  + [F-12] policy output is cited as observation or physical provenance

& [VerificationProgram] is ordered
  + [V-01] verify both source manifests against exact bytes and SHA-256
  + [V-02] verify replacement signature protocol, supersession, and binding table
  + [V-03] run nine focused unit tests in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [V-04] run the independent static no-effect test in both profiles
  + [V-05] verify production module hash remains 19AD251C59F313F74B159D5D68A59A6861E799DF5ACC7E19F93B226ED43EA0CD
  + [V-06] regenerate evidence with the replacement signature
  + [V-07] run evidence rehash tests in both profiles
  + [V-08] run workspace debug and overflow-checked release tests
  + [V-09] run format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and dependency audit
  + [V-10] publish corrected solution, proof, review, narrative, reentry, and evidence bindings

& [SemanticRefinementTrace] is exact
  + [policy] means interpretation of supplied syntax, not observation
  + [admitted] means valid under this profile, not safe, trusted, fresh, physically present, or Git-equivalent
  + [exact] means no normalization, no default, and no unknown-field tolerance
  + [valid_signature] means processed under the governing SJS protocol with externally bound stage evidence

& [ConstraintCheckTrace] is grounded
  + [source] preserves exact attribute, case, component, ordering, and zero-effect intent
  + [framework] requires protocol ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
  + [artifact_guard] requires separate evidence for each processed stage
  + [implementation] matches the intended profile and remains byte-identical
  + [conflict_repair] replaces authority lineage only and does not retrofit pre-implementation authorization

& [PruningTrace] removes overreach
  + [pruned] treating either local protocol UUID as governing SJS authority
  + [pruned] rewriting history to claim valid authority preceded implementation
  + [pruned] new policy semantics or profile version
  + [pruned] observation, trust, safety, physical, traversal, Git, receipt, and mutation claims
  + [pruned] decorative expansion without a requirement, constraint, fault, proof, or relation gain

& [FoldTrace] is seven-fold
  + [fold_1_subject] separates authority correction from behavior change
  + [fold_2_terms] fixes policy, admitted, exact, and valid-signature meanings
  + [fold_3_data] closes inputs, decision, fault, lifecycle, and absent state
  + [fold_4_relations] cross-weaves topology, parser, assembly, tests, and evidence
  + [fold_5_constraints] preserves twelve source and effect guards
  + [fold_6_failures] exposes twelve invalidation paths
  + [fold_7_proof] binds ten verification gates and historical supersession

& [GrowthSeedSet] is bounded
  + [seed_1] is supplied entry-observation assembly after corrected prerequisite authority
  + [seed_2] is a reusable repository SJS signature-protocol linter under separate source and authority
  - never: treat either seed as completed by this correction

& [ExhaustionReview] is phase locked
  + [source_preservation] complete
  + [behavior_boundary] complete
  + [authority_correction] complete
  + [data_design] complete
  + [constraint_and_pruning] complete
